        "tree_id": "8bb1c43c8f26f1c127591dddeffdead2b5094eb7",
        "message": "Fermat's Last Theorem in Lean 4 (Lean 4.33.1, Mathlib v4.33.0)\n\nA complete machine-checked proof of Fermat's Last Theorem: the import\nclosure of FinalCheck.lean - 1,450 definition modules (Definitions/),\n29,511 statement modules (Theorems/), 29,511 proof modules (P2M/Sol/),\nP2M/Util.lean, one derive module - on toolchain leanprover/lean4:v4.33.1\nwith Mathlib tag v4.33.0 (db584cd6d46c92f209a44c0f1c829460d327499d).\nFinalCheck.lean pins '#print axioms fermat_last_theorem' to [propext,\nClassical.choice, Quot.sound] and derives Mathlib's FermatLastTheorem\nfrom it.\n\nThis is the port to Lean 4.33.1 of the proof first checked on Lean\n4.30.0. Against the 4.30.0 text the only changes are the Mathlib renames\nand mechanical proof repairs the newer Mathlib required (about 9,200\nmodules differ in text); the theorem proved, the axioms it rests on and\nthe structure of the argument are unchanged. Checks on exactly these\nsources: the full build succeeds with the axiom list above; the comparator\n(leanprover/comparator v4.33.0) accepts the solution against a challenge\nfile that states the theorem citing only Mathlib - statement identity,\npermitted axioms, and a replay of the whole environment in the Lean kernel;\nnanoda, an independent kernel implementation, accepts the same\nenvironment. README.md gives the results and how to re-run them\n(verification/comparator/run.sh, verification/nanoda/run.sh);\nPROOF-PATH.md names each step of the argument and the Lean theorem that\ncarries it; NOTICE and ATTRIBUTION.md carry the licence and the\nthird-party attribution (Imperial College London FLT project,\nflt-regular, Mathlib); formalization.yaml records the project\nmetadata.\n\nAlso included: html/, a set of static web pages presenting the proof\n(open html/index.html in a browser; no server or network needed), and\ntools/docs-site/, the program that generated them from the Lean sources.",
